{"name":"Nuts and Bolts","hex":"#898c92","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"nuts and bolts","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The basic inner workings of something; the fundamentals; that which makes something operate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nuts_and_bolts"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nut (hardware)","blocks":[{"text":"A nut is a type of fastener with a threaded hole. Nuts are almost always used in conjunction with a mating bolt to fasten multiple parts together. The two partners are kept together by a combination of their threads' friction with slight elastic deformation, a slight stretching of the bolt, and compression of the parts to be held together."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/M4_Inbusschraube_focusstacked.jpg/330px-M4_Inbusschraube_focusstacked.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nut_(hardware)","wikidata":"Q190977"},{"title":"Nuts and Bolts (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Nuts and Bolts was a weekly television drama series, set in the fictional South Wales town of Ystrad. It began airing in 1999 on HTV. It ran for three years until it was cancelled in 2002."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nuts_and_Bolts_(TV_series)","wikidata":"Q7070541"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/SydneyHarbourBridgeNutMilsonsPoint.JPG/500px-SydneyHarbourBridgeNutMilsonsPoint.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/SydneyHarbourBridgeNutMilsonsPoint.JPG/1280px-SydneyHarbourBridgeNutMilsonsPoint.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/SydneyHarbourBridgeNutMilsonsPoint.JPG/500px-SydneyHarbourBridgeNutMilsonsPoint.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_con